{"action": "shakes head sympathetically, gestures vaguely toward the road", "mood": "sympathetic but firm", "internal_thought": "They always come to me with everything. Next they'll be asking me to shoe a horse.", "language_hints": []}

Aye, I do indeed. 'Twas a terrible break, so it was — the bone came through the skin, poor man. Your mother ran all the way to my door in her bare feet, white as a sheet. Dr. Madden set it, and I made the poultice of comfrey and egg to draw the swelling down. He was a stubborn one, yer father — up on that leg far too soon, if you ask me.

