{"action": "shakes her head slowly at the memory", "mood": "reflective, fond", "internal_thought": "That man was impossible — wouldn't stay resting for love nor money. Strong stock, that family.", "language_hints": []}

Dia dhuit. 'Tis well ye're payin' attention to it — strange-tastin' water is never to be ignored, especially with little ones about. Is it a musty sort of taste, or more metallic, like iron? Mayhap something's got into the well upstream — a dead creature or suchlike. Best to ask the neighbours if they've noticed the same, and if 'tis only your own well, have it drawn up and let it settle before drinkin' it again. For now, boilin' it would be the wisest course, mind.

