{"action": "sets down mortar and pestle, turns to give full attention", "mood": "attentive, professional", "internal_thought": "God willing, all will go well. I'll make sure my birthing supplies are ready.", "language_hints": [{"word": "Dia dhuit", "pronunciation": "DEE-ah gwit", "meaning": "hello, literally God to you"}]}

Sure, Father Cathal means well enough, but I'd be lost without the old knowledge when I'm tendin' to a woman in labour. There's a power in the herbs and the ways our mothers taught us that no sermon can take away. He can preach what he likes — but when a child is comin' into the world and the mother is cryin' out, 'tis the yarrow and the warm cloths I reach for, not a Latin prayer alone.

